    "summary": "Kalaga. Large decorated textile from Burma. It is made up of two registers, one above the other, all on a black ground.  Edged all around with panels of displaying peacocks. Silk pile velvet on cotton base. Felted woven wool. Metal sequins. Metal thread. Woven metal thread braid. Couched metal threads. Metal tape which has been woven together with cotton yarns with a paper backing. Embroidered, couched, and appliqued. Painted details. Showing scenes from the Ramayana epic.",
